cited": true}\n\ndata: {"event": "token", "delta": "### Phase Discontinuity vs Metric Projection (test fixture)\n\nThe epistemological evaluation of synthetic cognitive emergence features clear tension:\n\n1. **Discontinuous Transition Model:** Earlier hypothesis posits sudden jump dynamics once parameter scale crosses critical threshold thresholds [[c:0]].\n2. **Continuous Metric Model:** Systematic evaluation demonstrates that apparent discrete jumps are evaluation artifacts created by step-threshold scoring metrics [[c:1]].\n\nCurrent empirical synthesis strongly indicates smooth scaling dynamics rather than true physical phase jumps."}\n\ndata: {"event": "audit", "answer_final": "### Phase Discontinuity vs Metric Projection (test fixture)\n\nThe epistemological evaluation of synthetic cognitive emergence features clear tension:\n\n1. **Discontinuous Transition Model:** Earlier hypothesis posits sudden jump dynamics once parameter scale crosses critical threshold thresholds [[c:0]].\n2. **Continuous Metric Model:** Systematic evaluation demonstrates that apparent discrete jumps are evaluation artifacts created by step-threshold scoring metrics [[c:1]].\n\nCurrent empirical synthesis strongly indicates smooth scaling dynamics rather than true physical phase jumps.", "confidence": 0.62, "tier_agreement": "conflicting", "claims": [{"claim_id": 0, "text": "Discontinuous Transition Model: Earlier hypothesis posits sudden jump dynamics once parameter scale crosses critical threshold thresholds.", "status": "partially_supported", "citation_ids": [0], "supported": false, "evidence": "Synthetic neural competencies exhibit sharp first-order phase transitions occurring strictly when network parameter mass surpasses critical threshold theta (test fixture).", "note": "Contested by newer continuous metric geometry evaluations (test fixture).", "start": 150, "end": 303}, {"claim_id": 1, "text": "Continuous Metric Model: Systematic evaluation demonstrates that apparent discrete 